# Playwright Automation JS

A Playwright automation testing project using **JavaScript** for web UI and end-to-end (E2E) testing.

## 📌 Project Overview

This repository contains automated test cases developed using **Playwright with JavaScript**. The project is created for learning, practicing, and building practical automation testing skills.

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

* **Language:** JavaScript
* **Automation Tool:** Playwright
* **Runtime:** Node.js
* **Test Runner:** Playwright Test
* **IDE:** Visual Studio Code
* **Version Control:** Git & GitHub

## 📂 Project Structure

```text
playwright-automation-js/
│
├── tests/
│   ├── login.spec.js
│   ├── products.spec.js
│   └── ...
│
├── playwright.config.js
├── package.json
├── package-lock.json
└── README.md
```

## 🚀 Getting Started

### 1. Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/<your-username>/playwright-automation-js.git
```

### 2. Navigate to the Project

```bash
cd playwright-automation-js
```

### 3. Install Dependencies

```bash
npm install
```

### 4. Install Playwright Browsers

```bash
npx playwright install
```

## ▶️ Run Tests

Run all Playwright tests:

```bash
npx playwright test
```

Run tests with browser visible:

```bash
npx playwright test --headed
```

Run a specific test file:

```bash
npx playwright test tests/login.spec.js
```

Run tests in debug mode:

```bash
npx playwright test --debug
```

## 📊 View Test Report

After test execution:

```bash
npx playwright show-report
```

## 🧪 Testing Areas

The project covers practical Playwright automation concepts such as:

* Web UI automation
* Login testing
* Product selection
* Cart validation
* Form handling
* Locators
* Assertions
* Browser and page handling
* Wait mechanisms
* Multiple elements handling
* Test hooks
* Screenshots
* Trace viewer
* Data-driven testing
* End-to-end testing

## 🔍 Example Test

```javascript
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('Verify page title', async ({ page }) => {
    await page.goto('https://example.com');

    await expect(page).toHaveTitle(/Example/);
});
```

## 📸 Reports & Debugging

Playwright provides useful debugging features including:

* HTML reports
* Screenshots
* Videos
* Traces
* Debug mode

These features help identify and troubleshoot automation failures.

## 🎯 Project Goals

The main objectives of this project are:

1. Learn Playwright automation using JavaScript.
2. Understand Playwright locators and assertions.
3. Build reusable automation scripts.
4. Practice real-world E2E testing scenarios.
5. Develop a maintainable automation framework.
6. Improve automation testing skills for QA roles.

